As a child, Irelia watched her entire family be killed in front of her by invaders from Noxus. Their bodies lie in unmarked graves amongst swathes of other victims. Irelia swore that day to hone her skills as a blade dancer: a warrior that commands flying swords with the magic of telekinetic dance. She would take revenge on those that sought to burn her homeland of Ionia.

Irelia became the leader of a resistance whose only purpose was to drive out the Noxian invaders and free the people of Ionia. Though the defence of Ionia was successful, the land has been broken by the invasion, its people fragmented. People still look to Irelia for guidance and wisdom, but whilst some might welcome such power and responsibility, it only makes Irelia feel uneasy.

Irelia is a slender, pale-skinned woman with long dark hair up to the hips and sea green eyes . Her robes are a mix of elegant robes and battle attire with a distinctive palette of red, pink, black and silver. The most characteristic ornaments of her attire are the silver diadem on her head. She also has several silver blades that float around it.

Spiritualist: Irelia has a deep connection to the Spirit Realm, created through meditation and spiritual pratices, allowing her to sense the influences of the Spirit Realm, and use it's magic for several purposes. Irelia has nurtured that connection with the pratice of the dancing arts of her people.
Blade Silk Dance: Irelia has been trained in the tradicional dances of her people. More than simple exercises of artistic expression, these dances connect the dancer to the Spirit Realm, allowing it's power to flow through them.
Telekinesis: By dancing, Irelia can levitate her Crests Blades through dancing to use them in combat. It's unknown if she levitate objects without dancing, or levitate other objects besides her Blades
